{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And you shall observe.</b> Many thought that the placing of the blood on the lintel and on the two doorposts is an obligation for all generations, because \"this thing\" is adjacent to the taking of the hyssop and its dipping, and furthermore it is written afterward, \"where He passed over the houses of the children of Israel\" (Exodus 12:27). And by way of reasoning it would be correct, were it not for the received truth that is fully established. Rather, the correct view is that the phrase \"this thing\" refers back to \"and you shall slaughter the paschal offering,\" and the reason for the children's question is their seeing the entire family gathered as one group eating an unblemished lamb, its head on its legs and on its innards, breaking no bone in it, with no foreigner, resident, uncircumcised one, or hired laborer eating of it — and this is not the practice on other festivals:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:45.737828160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}